course: dictionary
lesson: 11155
title: When a word wilts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one to use. Wilt is one of them. «Van Gogh painted sunflowers at every stage, from fresh to wilting.» The flowers in these paintings look droopy and tired, so wilting must mean drooping and going soft.
explain: Plants wilt when they are short of water. «Water inside plant cells pushes outwards and keeps stems firm, like air in a balloon; without enough water the plant wilts.» If a plant looks floppy, ask yourself: has it had enough water?
explain: People can wilt too. In hot weather you may feel tired and weak, and we say you wilt. Old texts use wilt in a different way: the King James Bible has «thou wilt», which means «you will». Check the clues: is the word about a plant, a person, or an old text?
fact: Wilt is a verb: wilt, wilts, wilted, wilting.
fact: «Wilt» means to droop and become soft and floppy, usually because a plant needs water or is too hot.
fact: «Wilt» can also mean to become tired and weak, especially in heat.
fact: In old texts, «thou wilt» means «you will».
fact: Water fills the cells of a plant and keeps its stems firm, so without enough water the plant wilts.
exercise: «The lettuce left in the sun began to wilt.» What does wilt mean here? | Shine brightly like glass | Turn into a flower | Grow very tall and strong | *Droop and go soft and floppy
exercise: In an old Bible, a verse says «thou wilt». What does it mean? | *You will | You are finished | You have been to church | You are wet through
exercise: Sam says, «After the long hot walk I feel wilted.» What does wilted suggest? | Full of energy and ready to run | *Tired and weak from the heat | Very cold and shivering | Covered in water
test: «Van Gogh painted the flowers at every stage, from fresh to wilting.» Which word tells you the flowers were drooping? | sunflowers | fresh | *wilting | painted
test: Which meaning fits best when a person wilts in the heat? | *Becomes tired and weak | Becomes rich and famous | Becomes bright and loud | Becomes a loud shout
exam: Maya's plant wilts on the windowsill. What should she check first? | Whether the window is made of wood | *Whether the plant has had enough water | Whether the pot has a name | Whether the plant is painted yellow
